WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.305
A pure Rust

00:00:01.117 --> 00:00:02.720
GIS ships 300

00:00:02.532 --> 00:00:03.533
pull requests

00:00:04.062 --> 00:00:05.453
RustGIS is a

00:00:05.265 --> 00:00:07.175
free open-source GIS

00:00:06.998 --> 00:00:07.977
written in pure

00:00:07.788 --> 00:00:08.767
Rust that runs

00:00:08.579 --> 00:00:09.474
on Windows

00:00:09.522 --> 00:00:11.137
macOS Linux and

00:00:10.949 --> 00:00:11.774
in the browser

00:00:11.845 --> 00:00:12.929
with data staying

00:00:12.741 --> 00:00:13.684
on your machine

00:00:14.206 --> 00:00:16.658
Version 0.8.0 brings

00:00:16.470 --> 00:00:17.496
together more than

00:00:17.307 --> 00:00:18.922
300 pull requests

00:00:18.734 --> 00:00:20.196
from 20 contributors

00:00:20.291 --> 00:00:21.422
and keeps every

00:00:21.234 --> 00:00:22.095
layer in its

00:00:21.954 --> 00:00:23.356
own coordinate system

00:00:23.894 --> 00:00:24.872
It adds picture

00:00:24.684 --> 00:00:26.181
markers charts and

00:00:25.993 --> 00:00:27.007
curved labels in

00:00:26.819 --> 00:00:27.537
layouts

00:00:27.632 --> 00:00:28.882
new formats like

00:00:28.729 --> 00:00:30.745
GRIB and GeoPDF

00:00:30.899 --> 00:00:31.983
and an AI

00:00:31.795 --> 00:00:32.809
assistant that can

00:00:32.620 --> 00:00:33.127
look at the

00:00:32.939 --> 00:00:33.516
map

00:00:34.038 --> 00:00:35.052
Full story on

00:00:34.863 --> 00:00:35.759
the dashboard
